{"name":"Delicate Prunus","hex":"#a95c68","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"prunus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of traditional decoration on porcelain that depicts the leaves and branches of the Chinese plum, Prunus mume."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prunus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus is a genus of flowering trees and shrubs from the rose family (Rosaceae) that produce stone fruits, or drupes. As of March 2024, the genus has about 340 accepted species, including almonds, apricots, cherries, peaches, and plums. It has a cosmopolitan distribution, being native to the temperate regions of North America, the neotropics of South America, and temperate and tropical regions of Eurasia and Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg/330px-Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus","wikidata":"Q190545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/500px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/1280px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/500px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn